        "thinking": "I see. The adapters in `registry.ts` include:\n- `claudeLocalAdapter` - Claude (local subprocess or API)\n- `codexLocalAdapter` - OpenAI Codex \n- `openCodeLocalAdapter` - OpenCode\n- `piLocalAdapter` - Pi AI\n- `cursorLocalAdapter` - Cursor\n- `geminiLocalAdapter` - Gemini\n- `openclawGatewayAdapter` - Openclaw gateway\n\n\n- `hermesLocalAdapter` - Hermes\n- `processAdapter` - Generic process adapter\n- `httpAdapter` - HTTP adapter\n\nThese are all AI model adapters for connecting to different LLMs, not general-purpose service adapters. The user seems to be conflating these with storage adapters or other infrastructure adapters they might have in their Cloudflare environment, but the adapters here are specifically for routing requests to different AI models.\n\nThe issue is that some of these adapters like the local process ones rely on subprocess spawning, which won't work in Cloudflare Workers. In that environment, agent execution would need to happen through Durable Objects or Queues instead. I should check if the Cloudflare package has its own native adapter implementations, probably in the `adapter-executor/` directory.",
